B.boc=s(["During the first two weeks after the last menstrual period, egg follicles mature in the ovaries under the stimulus of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH), a hormone secreted by the pituitary gland in the brain.","High levels of the hormone estradiol, produced by the developing egg follicle, cause secretion of luteinizing hormone (LH), another hormone from the pituitary gland. LH triggers release of the egg from its follicle (ovulation).","For women with 28-day cycles, ovulation usually occurs on days 13 to 15."],t.s)
